        "buildJavaScript",
        "documentation"
      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "Follow these strict rules when generating code: use `getElementById` to select elements and do not use `querySelector`, `querySelectorAll`, arrays, loops, or advanced abstractions. Write separate named arrow functions for each button (`addButton1`, `addButton2`, `addButton3`) and attach them using `addEventListener`. Use a single variable called `cartTotal` to track the number of items in the cart.\n\nAll logic must be written using simple `if/else` statements only.\n\nWhen any add button is clicked, increase `cartTotal` by 1 and update the cart display. If `cartTotal` is greater than 0, show the cart button and update the cart badge text to match the current total. If `cartTotal` is equal to 0, hide the cart button.\n\nDo not use helper files, extra functions beyond what is necessary, class toggling, or unnecessary features. Do not use `classList`. Modify styles directly (for example, `cartButton.style.visibility = \"hidden\"` or `\"visible\"`).\n\nKeep the code short, direct, and beginner-friendly. Return complete JavaScript for all three buttons and the cart logic, not a partial example."
      }
    }
  },
